                <pb facs="0680" n="568" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg568"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.515/497: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-04T18:00:00-05:00">April 4, 1935—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>78. Your 153, April 1, 6 p.m.<anchor n="81" xml:id="d539-f1"/> With references to
                    British hope that this and other governments will, like the British, send to
                    China an economic technician, it would assist Department, in its present
                    consideration of the matter, to receive replies if they can conveniently be had
                    to questions as follows: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Has British Government informed Chinese Government of contemplated
                            appointment of British economic technician and if so what are the views
                            of the Chinese Government in regard thereto?</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Has British Government definitely selected its representative and if
                            so whom and when will he proceed to China?</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Are the views of the French and the Japanese Governments as yet
                            available?</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
